# Normalise text to LF in the repository, so a Windows checkout cannot introduce a
# whitespace-only diff that CI's `ruff format --check` then reports as a formatting failure.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The corpus PDFs are generated, committed, and byte-compared in CI by
# tools/build_corpus.py --check. If git ever decided one of them was text and normalised its line
# endings, the comparison would fail on a checkout rather than on a real change — and the failure
# would look like a stale document. So git is told explicitly never to touch their bytes.
#
# This rule comes AFTER the wildcard on purpose: in .gitattributes the LAST matching rule wins, so
# with the order reversed `*` re-enables text conversion for PDFs and silently undoes this.
*.pdf -text -diff

# Screenshots of the running console, for the same reason and with the same ordering caveat.
*.png -text -diff
